        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00009",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00242:title:sect-00009-title",
            "text": "Conversion of Acid Chlorides into Alcohols: Reduction and Grignard Reaction"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00017",
              "segmentId": "m00242:para:para-00017"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00018",
              "segmentId": "m00242:para:para-00018"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00010",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00242:alt:fig-00010-alt",
                  "text": "The reaction shows benzoyl chloride with lithium aluminum hydride in ether (step 1) followed by treatment with acid (step 2) to give benzyl alcohol (ninety-six percent), where benzene is attached to a hydroxymethyl group."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_21_04_010.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00019",
              "segmentId": "m00242:para:para-00019"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00011",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00242:alt:fig-00011-alt",
                  "text": "Benzoyl chloride reacts with methylmagnesium bromide in ether to give acetophenone (intermediate). Further reaction with methylmagnesium bromide (step one) followed by treatment with acid (step two) gives 2-phenyl-2-propanol (ninety-two percent)."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_21_04_011.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00010",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00242:title:sect-00010-title",
            "text": "Conversion of Acid Chlorides into Ketones: Diorganocopper Reaction"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00020",
              "segmentId": "m00242:para:para-00020"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00012",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00242:alt:fig-00012-alt",
                  "text": "An acid chloride reacts with a diorganocuprate in ether to form an acyl diorganocopper intermediate, which goes on to produce a ketone."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_21_04_012.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00021",
              "segmentId": "m00242:para:para-00021"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00013",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00242:alt:fig-00013-alt",
                  "text": "The reaction of 2,4-dimethyl-2-hexenoyl chloride with lithium diethylcopper in ether at minus seventy-eight degrees Celsius gives 4,6-dimethyl-4-octen-3-one (ninety-two percent). The common name of the product is Manicone."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_21_04_013.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00022",
              "segmentId": "m00242:para:para-00022"
            }
          ]
        },
